From 7a7d972f95cb9b77434bb98345f2e0b56b1425f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C3=A9on=20Tiek=C3=B6tter?= <leon@tiekoetter.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 23:43:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add upstream connection rotation and recovery

Add an optional lifetime for reusable upstream HTTP clients. When the
configured lifetime expires, new requests use a fresh client while
responses already using the retired client are allowed to finish before
it is closed.

This also allows connection rotation without Companion's proxy or IPv6
block settings, which is useful when source-address rotation is handled
transparently by the host network.

Set networking.connection_rotation_ms, or
NETWORKING_CONNECTION_ROTATION_MS, to a positive number of milliseconds
to enable rotation. The default of 0 preserves the existing behavior.

Also add optional bounded recovery on fresh connections for upstream 403s
and connection failures. Playback retains the downstream response and resumes
failed video chunks from the next undelivered byte. Recovery is disabled by
default; configure networking.connection_recovery_attempts and
networking.connection_recovery_timeout_ms to enable it.

Include cancellation, pool cleanup, range validation, and regression tests
covering simulated failures and real HTTP connection replacement.
